Z||000000||80's BOY||06-03-2000||05:45 PM||||has anyone ever participated in the silverstate classic challenge?? it's a nevada race where they close off a highway and people drive as FAST AS THEY CAN GO to the other end of it. about 100 miles. i want to, but don't know what to expect. Nevada is a long way from texas to take a chance like that!! any info??||||reg||10
Z||000001||GT Bastard||06-04-2000||02:22 AM||||That would be a blast.  I would never risk my car unless I had a heavily built motor, race-tuned suspension, etc...  100 miles of high-speed driving would be a sure way to grenade your motor/tranny.  If I had my old 4-banger, I would do it!  Just wail on that little Iron Duck until she pops.  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||batboy||06-04-2000||09:26 AM||||I want to go to Montana. The open highways there have no speed limits except it must be reasonable for the conditions. In other words, if you're doing 120 MPH in the rain, a cop might ticket you because you're driving to fast due to weather. Last I heard highway deaths were up (duh!) and they were considering imposing speed limits again.<P>For sustained high speed driving, tires are critical. They must be in perfect condition and high speed rated. Triple digit speeds really heat up those tires and if one lets go, you are in a world of hurt.||||reg||1
Z||000003||80's BOY||06-05-2000||11:33 PM||||check it out, guys. it's a 3 day event, <BR>day 1: qualifying laps.. Las Vegas Speedway<P>day 2: Parade of cars..downtown Las Vegas Strip<P>day 3: race day...5 a.m.<P>you have several inspections for your vehicles you are driving. it's open to everyone. i can't believe nobody has heard of this. it's kinda dangerous like you said....the tires and all. someone dies every year i think. there's a video out on each year's event. look it up on the net. wish i could go!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000004||Robert||06-05-2000||11:48 PM||||One of my print customers did it a few years ago.  He drives a NSX.  He clams to have covered the 100 miles with an average speed of just under 160MPH. Didn’t even come in the top 10.  <BR> I remember reading about this “race”, after someone in a Countach “spun, crashed and burned”. (Helicopter talk). There was talk of banning this event because of safety.   Seems some of the drivers had never raced before.  I think it’s more of a race for the rich and famous anyway.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||80's BOY||06-05-2000||11:53 PM||||it's not actually THAT expensive, depending on your limitations for fun. i got a brochure last year but the 85 wasn't fully tuned yet. yes, i considered doing it. the fee was something like $500 or so but there was alot of television publicity and free stuff. just driving on the track would be cool enough for me. maybe one of these days. it's just hard to get out of Texas sometimes. this is one of them. so damn far!||||reg||1
Z||000006||BN Boomer||06-06-2000||12:00 AM||||I hate to burst your bubble, batboy, but Montana enacted a maximum speed limit last year, 75mph if I remember correctly. Even though my last two trips across Montana were in my Suburban that won't break 100mph thanks to it's speed limiter, it was still pretty fun. I distinctly remember the huge billboard as I-90 enters Montana from Idaho at the top of Lookout Pass that said "Welcome To Montana. Please Drive A Safe and Prudent Speed." I should have taken a picture of it. I'm sure it's gone now. Come to think of it, a Fiero would be awesome to drive through that pass, lots of really good twists and turns that slow most everyone else down. It was also kind of a wierd feeling overtaking State Troopers even when I was cruising at a relatively mild 75mph. Made you feel like they were waiting to pull you over.<P>Boy were those the days (only 3 years ago  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> ). Seattle, WA to Temple, TX, 2400 miles in less than 40 hours all by my wittle ol' self...||||reg||1
Z||000007||80's BOY||06-06-2000||12:06 AM||||I-10...now That's a straightaway to get on to!!! balls to the wall...GO TEXAS!!!||||reg||1
Z||000008||Robert||06-06-2000||12:26 AM||||You mean this sign,<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Montana.jpg">  <P>I was there two years ago, visiting my sister in Red Lodge.  The rental car would only go 85MPH.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Robert (edited 06-06-2000).]||||reg||1
